{"kind":"doc","route":"/guide/app/craft-service","title":"craftService","blocks":[{"t":"heading","level":1,"id":"craftservice","children":[{"t":"text","text":"craftService"}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"A service is a factory with a "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"name"}]},{"t":"text","text":" and a "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"scope"}]},{"t":"text","text":" — not a class. It packages"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"primitives and dependencies behind an explicit API, and keeps the whole"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"dependency graph visible to the compiler."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":""},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"Use it when"}]},{"t":"text","text":" a component or route needs an owned state/context service, or"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"when reusable domain logic should be composed by other services."},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"Use a small adapter when a dependency is owned by the runtime environment"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"rather than by your application."}]},{"t":"paragraph","children":[{"t":"text","text":"The contrast with "},{"t":"code","text":"inject(...)"},{"t":"text","text":" scattered across classes is the point:"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"dependencies here are explicit and "},{"t":"strong","children":[{"t":"text","text":"type-visible"}]},{"t":"text","text":", which is what the route DI"},{"t":"text","text":" "},{"t":"text","text":"check and the test registers read."}]},{"t":"code","lines":[{"tokens":[{"text":"import","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" { craftService } ","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":"from","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" "},{"text":"'@craft-ts/core'","kind":"punctuation"},{"text":";","kind":"punctuation"}]}],"filename":"","language":"typescript","numbered":false,"firstLine":1},{"t":"heading","level":2,"id":"what-a-service-exposes","children":[